WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.940
Republicans choose Jordan and Thune after the house's biggest defeat in decades, resetting who leads them. This is Omni View North America, episode 44. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that, Arctic Drilling, Old Convictions, the Justice Department wants dismissed, and a crash in Los Angeles, then Progress Watch. The New York Times reports the House Republicans signaled they want fresh leadership, while Senate Republicans re-elected the leader they already have.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.500
Jordan and Thune are the two names the paper puts on those choices.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.540
One chamber is turning, the other is keeping the same hand on the gavel.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.780
That is who speaks for Republicans in each chamber as the new Congress takes shape.

00:00:40.814 --> 00:00:44.034
Western Arctic drilling is the question in front of Prime Minister Mark Carney.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:49.114
The hub reports he is weighing an end to the offshore ban before it expires in 2028.

00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:54.574
CBC reports he says Ottawa is consulting on what happens to that Arctic oil and gas ban.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.414
The restriction is still in force.

00:00:56.414 --> 00:01:02.734
The choice is whether it stops early or runs out on that date, and the consultation is the step he says is open now.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:11.200
The Justice Department, NPR Reports, has moved to dismiss criminal convictions of former Trump adviser Steve Bannon and of the Oath Keepers.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.920
The Department says it is acting in the interests of justice. NPR reports that critics are crying foul.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:25.040
Those convictions are the results now being asked to come off the books. If the dismissals go through, that is what changes for Bannon and for the Oath Keepers.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.976
Los Angeles is where an SU jumped the curb near the North Hollywood metro station.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.256
The New York Times reports at least three pedestrians were killed.

00:01:33.716 --> 00:01:37.456
Authorities said at least three more were critically injured, and that the cause was not

00:01:37.456 --> 00:01:38.296
immediately clear.

00:01:38.776 --> 00:01:41.516
The dead and the critically injured are who this changes things for.

00:01:41.896 --> 00:01:43.936
On a sidewalk, the vehicle left the road to reach.

00:01:44.576 --> 00:01:49.176
Peter Dirkson is a 60-year-old retired Winnipeg police officer from Manitoba's interlake,

00:01:49.556 --> 00:01:52.676
and Yahoo News Canada reports he has finished the hike he set himself.

00:01:52.676 --> 00:01:58.576
Nearly six months, more than 4,000 kilometers on the Pacific Crest Trail, on foot from the

00:01:58.576 --> 00:02:02.496
United States, Mexico border to Canada, to raise money for Ukraine's war.

00:02:02.936 --> 00:02:06.156
He started in early April and hit the northern end in late September.

00:02:06.676 --> 00:02:11.096
On October 5, a little more than a month after he finished, he said he never doubted he

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:11.596
would get there.

00:02:11.996 --> 00:02:12.636
Hard as it was.

00:02:13.096 --> 00:02:16.616
Nothing he went through, he said, matched what soldiers are suffering in Ukraine.

00:02:17.156 --> 00:02:21.396
The path starts near Campo, California and ends at Manning Provincial Park in British

00:02:21.396 --> 00:02:27.496
Columbia. A full crossing means 26 national forests in three American states. He averaged a marathon

00:02:27.496 --> 00:02:32.576
a day with as much as 50 pounds of gear, food and water on his back. The trail is officially

00:02:32.576 --> 00:02:40.056
about 4,265 kilometers. He figures he walked past 5,000, once fire closures, rerouts and supply

00:02:40.056 --> 00:02:44.896
runs are counted. Southern California heat, a black bear and her cubs in the Sierra Nevada,

00:02:45.396 --> 00:02:50.136
and Mount Whitney. The highest peak in the contiguous United States, on his 60th birthday,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.196
He watched helicopters lift other hikers off the trail.

00:02:53.676 --> 00:02:58.056
Chris Riley, who handles communications for the Pacific Crest Trail Association, called

00:02:58.056 --> 00:03:02.216
one continuous hike and audacious idea that very few try and fewer finish.

00:03:02.696 --> 00:03:05.576
About 5,000 people apply for permits in a typical year.

00:03:06.016 --> 00:03:09.036
Somewhere between 1,000 and 2,000 say they completed it.

00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:12.356
Only a tiny handful are true through hikers who skip nothing.

00:03:12.936 --> 00:03:15.996
His feet grew nearly three shoe sizes from swelling and calluses.

00:03:16.536 --> 00:03:18.836
Stress fractures and numb toes are still with him.

00:03:18.836 --> 00:03:22.716
Hikers called that Christmas toe, the hope-feeling returns by Christmas.

00:03:23.196 --> 00:03:28.056
He raised over $7,000 for two charities, one of them the Canada Ukraine Foundation.

00:03:28.696 --> 00:03:33.336
Valery Kostiuk, the foundation's executive director, said the point is larger than the

00:03:33.336 --> 00:03:33.496
check.

00:03:34.016 --> 00:03:35.096
It keeps Ukraine in view.

00:03:35.576 --> 00:03:39.976
The foundation has put more than $100 million in aid into Ukraine since the invasion.

00:03:40.456 --> 00:03:41.476
All of it from donations.

00:03:42.216 --> 00:03:46.416
Dirkson had about three years with the Royal Winnipeg Rifles Reserve, and on the Winnipeg

00:03:46.416 --> 00:03:49.636
police force he worked security, weapons handling and tactics.

00:03:50.116 --> 00:03:56.256
He went to Ukraine in September 2022 and stayed until September 2023, first in the international

00:03:56.256 --> 00:03:59.996
Legion for the Defense of Ukraine, then as a member of the Ukrainian Army.

00:04:00.456 --> 00:04:04.696
His brigade, he said, worked near the front and often took multiple casualties in a day.

00:04:05.296 --> 00:04:07.216
Soldiers he served with have written to thank him.

00:04:07.576 --> 00:04:11.616
He said he kept walking so people would remember Ukrainians still fighting to live peacefully

00:04:11.616 --> 00:04:12.156
and free.

